load @term/seed/code/structure/set
  find set

# A Kripke structure: a set of possible worlds linked by an accessibility relation, with each world labeled by which
# propositions hold there, the semantics of modal and temporal logic. Necessity means truth in all accessible worlds,
# possibility in some. It is the standard model for verifying that a system satisfies a temporal specification. The form
# carries the set of worlds; the accessibility relation and the labeling are the structure.
form kripke-structure
  link worlds, like set
